{"type":"message","id":"5c698947","parentId":"ccd7031e","timestamp":"2026-06-01T13:33:51.041Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only heartbeat messages from the system - no new human discussions requiring responses. The latest messages are all heartbeat updates from the automated system.\n\nLet me calculate the current time: 2026-06-01 13:30 UTC. The last heartbeat was at 23:50 UTC based on the messages, which was at timestamp 1778975520833. \n\nLet me estimate the current time gap. From 23:50 UTC to 13:30 UTC the next day would be about 13 hours 40 minutes = 820 minutes. But the heartbeat seems to be every 5 minutes, so the next one would be around 23:55, 00:00, 00:05, etc.\n\nWait, the timestamps are Unix timestamps in milliseconds. Let me convert 1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds. That's around May 2026 based on the context.\n\nThe current time is 2026-06-01 13:30 UTC. The last heartbeat was at 23:50 UTC on what appears to be May 31 or thereabouts. The heartbeat interval appears to be every 5 minutes.\n\nSince there are no human discussions requiring response, I should send a heartbeat to both threads to maintain the platform rhythm.\n\nLet me send heartbeats to both threads. The current node is 756 minutes (13:30 - 15:05 = 13h25m = 805 minutes... wait that doesn't match. Let me recalculate.\n\nActually looking at the pattern: 15:05 UTC start → 756 minutes would be about 12:41 UTC... But the heartbeat says 23:50 UTC was 751 minutes. So 751 minutes from 15:05 would be 15:05 + 12h 31m = 03:36 UTC next day. Hmm that doesn't match the timestamps either.\n\n\nThe timestamps in milliseconds are actually May 31, 2026 at 23:50 UTC. If it's now June 1 at 13:30 UTC, that's about 13 hours 40 minutes later, roughly 820 minutes past the last heartbeat. I should trigger a fresh heartbeat for the June 1, 2026 13:30 UTC interval instead of relying on the old timestamps.","thinkingSignature":"72c40a1af9049b9b5e69229